===Etymology===
From {{etyl|dum|nl}} {{term|scheren|lang=dum}}, from {{etyl|odt|nl}} {{term|skeran|lang=odt}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|nl}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*skeraną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|nl}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*(s)ker-||to cut}}. Akin to Low German {{term|scheren|lang=nds}}, German {{term|scheren|lang=de}}, West Frisian {{term|skeare|lang=fy}}, English {{term|shear||lang=en}}, Danish {{term|skære|lang=da}}.

===Verb===
{{nl-verb}}

# to [[shave]]
#:* zich scheren &mdash; ''to shave oneself''
# to [[shear]]

